From 240976a50c3d391e3b242fdb3ad947757dc3aadd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macmanes <macmanes@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:43:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Build debug messages only when they print

debugMes() tested the verbosity level after its caller had already built
the message, and many messages call SeqVertex.toString(), which averages
the vertex's weight vector. That was most of Butterfly's CPU on typical
Trinity phase-2 graphs. Each call is now guarded by the same level test
debugMes applies (mechanical rewrite; messages with side effects would
have been skipped, none were found).
